<%--
Feature_Reference - Ouro compiler, tooling, and project chapters.
--%>
<Define:Feature_Reference>
  <section
    id="check-evaluate"
    class="docs-section"
    data-search-section
    aria-labelledby="check-evaluate-title"
  >
    <h2 id="check-evaluate-title">Check & Evaluate</h2>
    <p>
      <code>check</code> resolves imports and typechecks the complete module closure.
      <code>eval</code> evaluates a declaration or expression after checking its declared type.
    </p>
    <pre class="docs-code" data-language="terminal"><code>sh scripts/ouro1.sh check samples/tutorial/02_nat.ouro
sh scripts/ouro1.sh eval samples/examples/nat.ouro --print four
sh scripts/ouro1.sh eval samples/examples/nat.ouro --eval 'add four two'</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section
    id="native-builds"
    class="docs-section"
    data-search-section
    aria-labelledby="native-builds-title"
  >
    <h2 id="native-builds-title">Native Builds</h2>
    <p>
      The implemented native path extracts Ouro source to C and links it with the repository
      runtime. It is aimed at short-lived command-line programs, not general deployment yet.
    </p>
    <pre class="docs-code" data-language="terminal"><code>sh scripts/build_tool.sh samples/demo/01_hello.ouro _build/tools/hello
./_build/tools/hello</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section
    id="formatter-linter"
    class="docs-section"
    data-search-section
    aria-labelledby="formatter-linter-title"
  >
    <h2 id="formatter-linter-title">
      Formatter & Linter
    </h2>
    <p>
      The conservative formatter preserves comments and hand-aligned continuations. The compiler
      linter parses individual Ouro files and reports source-level rules separately from analysis.
    </p>
    <pre class="docs-code" data-language="terminal"><code>sh scripts/ouro1.sh fmt --check path/to/module.ouro
sh scripts/ouro1.sh fix --check path/to/module.ouro
sh scripts/ouro1.sh lint std samples</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section
    id="analyzer"
    class="docs-section"
    data-search-section
    aria-labelledby="analyzer-title"
  >
    <h2 id="analyzer-title">Analyzer</h2>
    <p>
      The repository analyzer covers architecture, dead code, API surface, trust policy, metrics,
      dataflow, effects, taint, duplication, and other opt-in structured families. Analyzer success
      is quality evidence, not kernel acceptance.
    </p>
    <pre class="docs-code" data-language="terminal"><code>sh scripts/ouro1.sh analyze --strict
sh scripts/ouro1.sh analyze --help</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section
    id="tests"
    class="docs-section"
    data-search-section
    aria-labelledby="tests-title"
  >
    <h2 id="tests-title">Tests</h2>
    <p>
      Ouro includes user tests, golden-output comparisons, accepted and rejected source fixtures,
      kernel corpora, protocol suites, and repository gates. A skipped suite is not a pass.
    </p>
    <pre class="docs-code" data-language="terminal"><code>sh scripts/ouro1.sh test samples/examples/test_demo.ouro</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section
    id="packages"
    class="docs-section"
    data-search-section
    aria-labelledby="packages-title"
  >
    <h2 id="packages-title">Packages</h2>
    <p>
      The experimental package tool resolves a local directory registry, vendors ordinary Ouro
      source into <code>_ouro_pkgs/</code>, and records deterministic contents in a lockfile. It does
      not fetch from a public network registry.
    </p>
    <pre class="docs-code" data-language="terminal"><code>sh scripts/ouro1.sh pkg init
sh scripts/ouro1.sh pkg add NAME --range '^0.1.0'
sh scripts/ouro1.sh pkg install
sh scripts/ouro1.sh pkg verify</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section
    id="documentation"
    class="docs-section"
    data-search-section
    aria-labelledby="documentation-title"
  >
    <h2 id="documentation-title">Documentation</h2>
    <p>
      The documentation generator extracts declaration-adjacent comments and creates one Markdown
      page per module. The generated standard-library reference is committed under
      <code>docs/api/</code>.
    </p>
    <pre class="docs-code" data-language="terminal"><code>sh scripts/ouro1.sh doc --out _build/api std/io.ouro</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section
    id="lsp-vscode"
    class="docs-section"
    data-search-section
    aria-labelledby="lsp-vscode-title"
  >
    <h2 id="lsp-vscode-title">LSP & VS Code</h2>
    <p>
      The experimental language server provides diagnostics, hover, definitions, completion,
      symbols, rename, and formatting. The VS Code extension adds syntax highlighting and an LSP
      client for trusted workspaces.
    </p>
    <pre class="docs-code" data-language="terminal"><code>sh scripts/ouro1.sh lsp</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section
    id="architecture-kernel"
    class="docs-section"
    data-search-section
    aria-labelledby="architecture-kernel-title"
  >
    <h2 id="architecture-kernel-title">
      Architecture & Kernel
    </h2>
    <p>
      Ouro separates the larger frontend, C backend, runtime, caches, and tools from a small
      hand-written OCaml kernel. The kernel validates and checks versioned core declarations; it
      does not prove compiler correctness, runtime safety, or the truth of explicit axioms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section
    id="stability-roadmap"
    class="docs-section"
    data-search-section
    aria-labelledby="stability-roadmap-title"
  >
    <h2 id="stability-roadmap-title">
      Stability & Roadmap
    </h2>
    <p>
      Ouro is pre-1.0 research software. Syntax, standard-library APIs, package files, CLI behavior,
      editor integration, and runtime coverage may change. The current direction is a coherent,
      reproducible public development release before broader language growth.
    </p>
  </section>
</Define:Feature_Reference>
